WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:03.690
Let's go to our caller from the five or eight
area code.

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:07.130
Maybe a caller from the Boston area.

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:08.170
Caller from five 08.

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:09.170
What's your name?

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:10.280
Where are you calling from?

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.120
Hello, David.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:13.120
Yes.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:15.340
This is tell me from Massachusetts.

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:17.759
Toby, how are you?

00:00:17.759 --> 00:00:18.759
I'm doing good.

00:00:18.759 --> 00:00:20.289
My question to you is.

00:00:20.289 --> 00:00:26.369
Do you think Republicans will be onboard with
abolishing the Electoral College if they lose

00:00:26.369 --> 00:00:28.119
an election?

00:00:28.119 --> 00:00:32.619
If if they win the popular vote, but lose
the Electoral College.

00:00:32.619 --> 00:00:34.750
Well, so two answers to that.

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:35.750
First is.

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:40.300
Yeah, probably they'll probably very quickly
change their mind if the Electoral College

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:41.339
ends up hurting them.

00:00:41.339 --> 00:00:43.960
So Republicans benefit from the Electoral
College.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:49.579
We have a number of cases, including in 2016,
where the Republican candidate lost the popular

00:00:49.579 --> 00:00:51.059
vote but won electorally.

00:00:51.059 --> 00:00:53.430
And that's part of why Republicans defend
it.

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:55.260
But it's extremely unlikely to happen.

00:00:55.260 --> 00:01:01.120
That's the reality and that many Republican
presidents have only won because of the Electoral

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:02.120
College.

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:04.320
And I mean, listen, this November is an example.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:06.060
Trump is not going to win the popular vote.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:09.500
The question is, did he does he eke out an
electoral victory?

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:11.740
So I just don't think we're going to see that
anytime soon.

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:16.030
I mean, maybe, you know, in four or eight
years, but certainly this year, Biden.

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:20.060
If I were a betting man, I would bet on Biden
winning the popular vote.

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:22.330
I don't know who's going to win electorally.

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:25.939
Yeah, because that's something I've been thinking
about.

00:01:25.939 --> 00:01:28.570
I would think about the.

00:01:28.570 --> 00:01:32.229
The national popular vote interstate compact
that I'm in.

00:01:32.229 --> 00:01:38.960
I've been hoping then that is something that
gets through in the near future, even if it's

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:42.240
not likely because.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:44.409
The Electoral College is such a broken system.

00:01:44.409 --> 00:01:49.650
Yes, yes, so for people who don't know the
national popular vote interstate compact,

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:53.840
what that is, is essentially states who say.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:02:00.000
Instead of awarding our electoral votes to
whoever wins, our state will award them to

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.640
whoever wins the national popular vote.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:08.140
If you get enough states together to do that,
such that the total of their electoral votes

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:11.880
is 270, which is the number required for the
presidency.

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:16.000
You've effectively made a national popular
vote.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:22.770
The legal question around it is whether some
states are not allowed to do that.

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:27.600
And that's an issue that's come up recently
by state constitutional law.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.390
And obviously, you know, I'm not a lawyer.

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:31.530
My formal training is in podiatry.

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:34.720
So I would not be able to answer that.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:40.300
OK, I guess we lost Toby there, Toby.

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:42.660
Toby had enough with me and Toby hung up.

